<BaseLayout
  title="About — Mariana Ordonez"
  description="From a gastronomy degree to self-taught design to the Ferrero digital shelf, my own Shopify store, and AI experience design — the path, and why the e-commerce × AI intersection is where I do my best work."
  type="article"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hello, I'm Mariana.</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      I'm a product designer with 6+ years designing digital experiences for e-commerce and
      SaaS — now focused on AI-powered UX. I work at the intersection of user behavior, business
      goals, and emerging AI tools.
    </p>

    <p>
      I started in an unexpected place: a gastronomy degree at Universidad de La Sabana. It
      sounds like a detour, but the instinct turned out to be the same one I use every day now —
      designing how someone <em>experiences</em> a product, from the first impression to the last
      detail. I taught myself design, and I've been refining that instinct on real products ever
      since.
    </p>

    <h2>From e-commerce craft to scale</h2>

    <p>
      My roots are in e-commerce. I designed and branded a cycling-apparel line at Casabianca
      that drove a 25% sales increase, ran my own illustration store, and did end-to-end UX/UI
      for web products and digital tools. That work taught me how design decisions translate
      into conversion — and how to hold quality across many projects at once.
    </p>

    <p>
      Today I design the <a href="/work/ferrero-digital-shelf/">Ferrero digital shelf</a> —
      Nutella, Kinder, Tic Tac, Ferrero Rocher and more — across Amazon, Walmart, Target, Kroger,
      Instacart and other marketplaces. The job is translating strict global brand guidelines
      into platform-specific shopping experiences that perform at scale, in parallel, on deadline.
    </p>

    <p>
      In 2026 I opened my own shop,
      {' '}<a href="https://tienda.mordonez.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mariana Ordoñez Art</a>{' '}—
      original watercolors, limited editions, cards, downloads and commissions. I designed and coded
      it myself: a custom Shopify theme built with an AI-assisted workflow, a guided commission flow,
      and the CRO basics I'd recommend to any client. Running it end to end — merchandising,
      photography, copy, fulfillment — keeps me honest about what actually moves a shopper.
    </p>

    <h2>Why AI now</h2>

    <p>
      Working in high-volume content, I started bringing generative AI into my own creative
      workflow — to ship faster and at higher volume without losing brand craft. That's where I
      learned what these tools are genuinely good at, and where human judgment still has to lead.
    </p>

    <p>
      Now I'm focused on designing the AI products themselves: conversational interfaces,
      copilots, and systems where people need to understand, trust, and act on AI-generated
      output. I've grounded that focus with Google's Conversation Design Fundamentals and IBM's
      Generative AI for UI/UX. The through-line from food to product pages to AI interfaces is the
      same — design for the moment someone decides, and design for trust.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>

    <p>
      Research-driven, with a sharp eye for visual craft and fluency in English for cross-functional
      work with international teams. I care about evidence over adjectives, process over polish, and
      shipping on time without cutting corners.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>

    <p>
      I'm based in Bogotá and open to remote product- and AI-design roles with teams building the
      next generation of intelligent products. Reach me at
      {' '}<a href="mailto:marianaordonez04@gmail.com">marianaordonez04@gmail.com</a>{' '}
      or on <a href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>, or
      {' '}<a href="/Mariana-Ordonez-CV.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">view my CV (PDF)</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
